      "cat-harness:section": "2. The stub is NOT free of the definition's name",
      "prov:value": "### A third claim was here, and it was wrong"
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/source/concepts-harness/not-declared-yet.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A third claim was here, and it was wrong",
      "prov:value": "### A third claim was here, and it was wrong\n\nThis section listed the JSON-LD serialisation as a **MUST** carried by nothing.\nIt is carried by `coverage.serialisations` and checked by\n`check:subgraph-coverage` — and it is the **strictest** obligation in the set,\nthe only one `coverage.exempt` refuses to waive. The claim was made by reading\n`coverage` as three fields when it has four, which is the failure this page\nwarns about one section earlier: treating an overlapping set as the same set.\n\nIt is corrected rather than quietly deleted because a reader who saw the first\nversion would go looking for a gap that is not there, and because *\"stated as a\nMUST, carried by nothing\"* is the specific kind of error a page written in RFC\n2119 key words is most able to cause."
    }
  ]
}
